# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cutover working directory — never commit real migration data
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything a cutover reads or writes locally lives here: the source extract,
# the canonical bundle built from it, the manifest, the reject reports and the
# evidence artifacts. All of it is the client's live commercial data — buyer
# names, identity documents, bank references, contract values — and none of it
# belongs in a repository, on any branch, ever.
migration-work/

# The source extract itself, wherever somebody drops it. A workbook landing in
# the repository root and going in with `git add -A` is the realistic accident,
# and no spreadsheet is a legitimate fixture here: the canonical bundle is CSV
# and test data is Python.
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.xlsm

# NOT `*.csv`, deliberately. The canonical intake bundle is CSV, and the
# synthetic fixture — obviously fictional people, obviously fictional projects —
# is committed as CSV so the importer has something to be tested against.
# Ignoring the extension would silently exclude the one form of this data that
# is supposed to be here, and the exclusion would be discovered by its absence.
